                            <comment id="14696307" author="cos" created="Fri, 14 Aug 2015 01:35:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Is there any way to disable ignite-yarn module in 1.3.0 release so that it can be built and used at all?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14700608" author="cos" created="Tue, 18 Aug 2015 01:55:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Why adding a new version variable? It has a danger of building some modules against hadoop 2.7 and yarn module against bits from 2.7.1 - that leaves a bad aftertaste. Also, it means that downstream integrator (read Apache Bigtop) would have to set two different variables of they want to build against a non-default version of Hadoop.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14701998" author="cos" created="Tue, 18 Aug 2015 21:17:24 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Yeah, I am pretty convinced that there should be a better way of solving this: perhaps making Hadoop 2.7.0 as the requirement for Ignite 1.3+? Or dropping &lt;tt&gt;@Override&lt;/tt&gt; annotation all together from the line in question? This way it will get compiled just fine with Hadoop 2.6. What do you think?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mixing different versions of base hadoop and yarn would be a real bad idea. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
